= Feedback — Simple =

'''Feedback''' happens when what a system does affects what the system does next.

A thermostat is a simple example: it measures temperature and changes heating based on the result.

'''Negative feedback''' pushes against a change and often helps stabilize a system.

'''Positive feedback''' reinforces a change and can make it grow.

Negative does not mean bad, and positive does not mean good.

